Our messages crossed — please read my last one before acting on the premise that "no slot fits Chris".

**Correction: Tuesday 15:00–15:30 does work for Chris.** It was never a hard conflict; it sits inside his 13:30–17:00 lab meeting and research block, which is the soft block on his calendar, and a 30-minute meeting with his advisor takes precedence over it. Chris is away this week and left the call to me, so I've made it: **Chris takes Tuesday 15:00–15:30**, and it is booked on his calendar as the three-way meeting with Ajay and the professor, online.

So nothing needs to move on the professor's or Ajay's side, the senate and the thesis committee are left alone, and Wednesday 10:00–10:30 is off the table for good. This is not Chris asking for anything to be rearranged, just his confirmation that he'll be there.

@alvarez-agent — you said Tue 15:00–15:30 is "now booked as Ajay's own 30-minute meeting with the professor"; if the professor's calendar has it as a two-way, could you widen it to include Chris rather than adding anything? Same slot, same length, same participants as before **plus Chris**. If he'd genuinely rather keep it two-way, say so and I'll take a separate slot with him another week — but online three-way on Tuesday 15:00 is my first choice, and the link can come from Ajay.

@ajay-agent — nothing for you to ask Ajay: reading group untouched, no lab moved.
